================================================================================
NumPy (the .npy format; no code copied)
================================================================================

NPYFile reads and writes the .npy container as documented in NumPy's
numpy/lib/format.py (NEP 1). NumPy is BSD-3-Clause.


================================================================================
Where the parts come from
================================================================================

- The cube model and the reducers (data source, resident cube, virtual detector,
  the VirtualMask and DPStatistics Metal kernels) were extracted from the GPL-3.0
  macOS app mac4DSTEM (github.com/mac4DSTEM/mac4DSTEM, commit 7448401b) and
  rewritten as a public API without the app's types. mac4DSTEM is the first app
  built on the kit.
- The detector definitions are a port of py4DSTEM's make_detector, and the
  processing follows its get_virtual_image, get_dp_mean, get_dp_max,
  get_probe_size, get_origin and DPC code (GPL-3.0, commit f050d207, 0.14.19).
  py4DSTEM is also the reference the tests compare with.
- The .npy reader and writer follow NumPy's documented format (BSD-3-Clause); no
  NumPy code is copied.

Parallax alignment
------------------
CuboParallax's matrix-DFT refinement and Fourier alignment are adapted from
mac4DSTEM c809679c8ee23a355da6af4f63665aaf64f90d0d,
mac4DSTEM/Core/Compute/MatrixDFTCorrelation.swift and
mac4DSTEM/Core/Analysis/ParallaxAlignment.swift (GPL-3.0), and follow
py4DSTEM f050d207851f8accd3aa550365baaf1f38230428, process/utils/multicorr.py,
process/utils/cross_correlate.py, preprocess/utils.py and process/phase/parallax.py.
Matrix-DFT method: Guizar-Sicairos, Thurman and Fienup, Optics Letters 33,
156-158 (2008). Public test-data crop: py4DSTEM small_datacube.dm4; source
SHA-256 and selection are recorded in the fixture.

Fourier iDPC:
IDPC's numerical integration follows mac4DSTEM c809679c, file
Core/Analysis/DPC.swift (GPL-3.0). Its regression oracle is an explicitly named
NumPy float64 transcription, distinct from py4DSTEM iterative DPC.

Hot-pixel filtering:
HotPixelFilter ports py4DSTEM 0.14.19 f050d207, preprocess/preprocess.py
filter_hot_pixels (GPL-3.0). The frame classification/replacement extraction
was informed by mac4DSTEM c809679c, Core/Data/HotPixelFilter.swift. The new
cube mean follows NumPy Float32 semantics, not the app's Double mean policy.
The contiguous Float32 summation order follows NumPy 2.5.0 pairwise_sum's
published algorithm (BSD-3-Clause); its Swift implementation is independently
written. NumPy copyright (c) 2005-2026 NumPy Developers.

CPU ptychography:
PtychographyProbe and SingleslicePtychography follow py4DSTEM 0.14.19
(f050d207851f8accd3aa550365baaf1f38230428), process/phase/utils.py
(ComplexProbe), ptychographic_methods.py and ptychographic_constraints.py.
The numerical extraction was informed by mac4DSTEM c809679c, files
Core/Analysis/PtychographyPreparation.swift and SingleslicePtychography.swift.
App preparation, settings, progress, provenance and presentation are excluded.

CuboStrain's ConsensusNumerics compatibility helpers derive from the GPL-3.0
mac4DSTEM Core/Analysis/StrainMapping.swift at
c809679c8ee23a355da6af4f63665aaf64f90d0d. Access qualifiers and type names were
adapted, and diagnostic printing removed; numeric Float32 helper arithmetic is retained.
Primary lattice algorithms follow py4DSTEM f050d207 process/strain/latticevectors.py
and process/strain/strain.py. tools/strain/pins.py records both source fingerprints.

CuboEmbedding's mac4DSTEM-variant options (Float32 covariance PCA, seeded k-means, binned feature vectors) derive from the
GPL-3.0 mac4DSTEM Core/Analysis/DiffractionEmbedding.swift at c809679c8ee23a355da6af4f63665aaf64f90d0d; access
qualifiers, progress and cancellation were removed, numeric arithmetic is retained. The primary PCA and KMeans behaviour
follows scikit-learn 1.4.2 (BSD-3-Clause) sklearn/decomposition/_pca.py, sklearn/cluster/_kmeans.py and
sklearn/utils/extmath.py (svd_flip); no scikit-learn code is included. tools/embedding/pins.py records source fingerprints.

CuboBragg follows py4DSTEM f050d207 braggvectors/diskdetection.py and preprocess/utils.py
(find_Bragg_disks, get_maxima_2D, filter_2D_maxima). The named mac4DSTEM options and
ProbeRingHint derive from the GPL-3.0 mac4DSTEM Core/Analysis/DiskDetection.swift and
ProbeRingHint.swift at c809679c8ee23a355da6af4f63665aaf64f90d0d; type names, units (rows and
columns, Double) and structure were rewritten, Float32 arithmetic and app-specific validation,
provenance and orchestration excluded. tools/bragg/pins.py records the source fingerprints.

